abstract: >-
  MELITE is a pre-stable multi-model classifier evaluator for tabular
  classification, model selection with nested cross-validation, final model
  export, and artifact-based inference.

  It operates at the tabular modeling level by consuming numeric feature
  matrices and labels. MELITE evaluates SVC, Random Forest, XGBoost, and
  opt-in Stacking model families under an outer repeated-stratified
  cross-validation framework, with inner hyperparameter search for tunable
  families. It selects the best active family by mean outer-CV F1-macro,
  persists aggregate and per-fold evaluation evidence, and supports final
  model retraining, export, and artifact-based inference.
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - tabular classification
  - model evaluation
  - model selection
  - nested cross-validation
  - SVC
  - random forest
  - XGBoost
  - stacking
